rvice revenue. The Company recognized $6.7 million and $12.1 million in lease revenue during the three months ended September 26, 2026 and September 27, 2025, respectively. The Company recognized $27.6 million and $35.7 million in lease revenue during the nine months ended September 26, 2026 and September 27, 2025, respectively. The decrease in lease revenue was primarily due to the CDMO divestiture in the second quarter of 2026. Due to the nature of these arrangements and timing of the contractual lease term, the remaining revenue to be recognized related to these lease performance obligations is not material to the unaudited condensed consolidated financial statements. 15 CHARLES RIVER LABORATORIES INTERNATIONAL, INC. NOTES TO UNAUDITED CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS 4. SEGMENT AND GEOGRAPHIC INFORMATION The Company operates in three reportable segments: DSA, Manufacturing, and RMS. The reportable segments comprise the structure used by the Company\u2019s Chief Executive Officer, who is the Chief Operating Decision\n"}
